To date, forty-seven women and three men have been married to a [[British prime minister]] in office. There have also been four bachelor and nine widower prime ministers; the last bachelor was [[Edward Heath]] (1970–1974) and the last widower was [[Ramsay MacDonald]] (1924, 1929–1935). The [[Augustus FitzRoy, 3rd Duke of Grafton|Duke of Grafton]] (1768–1770) and [[Boris Johnson]] (2019–2022) are the only prime ministers to have divorced and remarried while in office.

The current prime minister, [[Andy Burnham]], has been married to [[Marie-France van Heel]] since 2000.
